#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Your device or source app sends data to Google Health. Nocturne reads the selected account through Google's API and stores supported records in this tenant's existing histories. A Google Cloud project provides permission to use the API; it does not generate health data."
msgstr "Your device or source app sends data to Google Health. Nocturne reads the selected account through Google's API and stores supported records in this tenant's existing histories. A Google Cloud project provides permission to use the API; it does not generate health data."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Open Settings → Connectors & Apps → Google Health. Keep the Google Cloud console in another tab. The reference panel below shows the callback path, requested read permissions, supported destinations, and default sync interval from this running version."
msgstr "Open Settings → Connectors & Apps → Google Health. Keep the Google Cloud console in another tab. The reference panel below shows the callback path, requested read permissions, supported destinations, and default sync interval from this running version."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Imported steps, heart rate, and sleep appear in their reports. Weight appears in Patient Record → Weight history. The supported-destinations table below follows the connector's actual capability catalogue."
msgstr "Imported steps, heart rate, and sleep appear in their reports. Weight appears in Patient Record → Weight history. The supported-destinations table below follows the connector's actual capability catalogue."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "The phone/watch must first sync to Google. Local Health Connect records do not guarantee availability in Google's cloud API. Inventory availability, Google sign-in, and import completion are separate states. Unsupported types can be visible but cannot be selected for import."
msgstr "The phone/watch must first sync to Google. Local Health Connect records do not guarantee availability in Google's cloud API. Inventory availability, Google sign-in, and import completion are separate states. Unsupported types can be visible but cannot be selected for import."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Create the Web application client"
msgstr "Create the Web application client"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Review the inventory and start an import"
msgstr "Review the inventory and start an import"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Ongoing sync and historical progress"
msgstr "Ongoing sync and historical progress"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Automatic sync uses the default interval shown below unless your server changes it. Managed imports resume recent data from a saved watermark with an overlap, then work backwards through older calendar months towards Import data from. Large or failing periods can be split into smaller windows. Progress describes stages and pages, not an exact remaining time. A restart resumes the saved cursor. Completed older months are not continually rescanned for data that Google uploads late."
msgstr "Automatic sync uses the default interval shown below unless your server changes it. Managed imports resume recent data from a saved watermark with an overlap, then work backwards through older calendar months towards Import data from. Large or failing periods can be split into smaller windows. Progress describes stages and pages, not an exact remaining time. A restart resumes the saved cursor. Completed older months are not continually rescanned for data that Google uploads late."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Data appeared in Google after an older month was completed"
msgstr "Data appeared in Google after an older month was completed"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "First confirm that Google now contains the records. Refresh inventory checks availability but does not refill a completed month. Ask a platform administrator to use Import recovery → Open connector reset, select the correct tenant and earliest date to re-read, and monitor the job. The normal import path updates records with duplicate protection. Do not delete all data to solve an empty date range."
msgstr "First confirm that Google now contains the records. Refresh inventory checks availability but does not refill a completed month. Ask a platform administrator to use Import recovery → Open connector reset, select the correct tenant and earliest date to re-read, and monitor the job. The normal import path updates records with duplicate protection. Do not delete all data to solve an empty date range."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Common setup errors"
msgstr "Common setup errors"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Pause, disconnect, and deletion"
msgstr "Pause, disconnect, and deletion"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Clear selected types and Save import settings to pause imports without deleting history. Disconnect removes the connection but keeps imported records. Delete imported Google data is a separate confirmed action available after disconnecting; it affects this tenant's imported records, not Google's originals. Credentials are stored in the server's encrypted connector configuration. Never paste the secret or token into support conversations."
msgstr "Clear selected types and Save import settings to pause imports without deleting history. Disconnect removes the connection but keeps imported records. Delete imported Google data is a separate confirmed action available after disconnecting; it affects this tenant's imported records, not Google's originals. Credentials are stored in the server's encrypted connector configuration. Never paste the secret or token into support conversations."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Google: API setup, access availability, and account linking"
