msgstr "Install Google Health and check your data"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Install Google Health (formerly Fitbit) using the Play Store link below. Open it, sign in with the Google account you want to share, and complete its profile setup. Before continuing, make sure the steps, heart rate, sleep, or weight you want to share are visible in that app. Signing into Google alone is not enough."
msgstr "Install Google Health (formerly Fitbit) using the Play Store link below. Open it, sign in with the Google account you want to share, and complete its profile setup. Before continuing, make sure the steps, heart rate, sleep, or weight you want to share are visible in that app. Signing into Google alone is not enough."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Install Google Health from the Play Store"
msgstr "Install Google Health from the Play Store"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Bring data from other apps into Google Health (optional)"
msgstr "Bring data from other apps into Google Health (optional)"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "On Android use Health Connect, Google's on-device data-sharing service. Let your source app write the desired records and let Google Health read them. In Google Health open Connections → Partner apps → Sync your favorite health apps → Set up. Review the data, history, and background permissions, then check that records appear in Google Health. Garmin needs its watch to sync to Garmin Connect first; Google Health does not connect directly to the watch. Google also documents Samsung Galaxy, Xiaomi/Mi Fitness, Oura, Whoop, Strava, and MyFitnessPal connections. On iPhone the route is generally Apple Health. Available types differ by app: a direct Strava connection exports Google Health activities to Strava; importing Strava activities uses Health Connect or Apple Health instead. Google Health supports more types than this Nocturne connector, so check the importable-type table below."
msgstr "On Android use Health Connect, Google's on-device data-sharing service. Let your source app write the desired records and let Google Health read them. In Google Health open Connections → Partner apps → Sync your favorite health apps → Set up. Review the data, history, and background permissions, then check that records appear in Google Health. Garmin needs its watch to sync to Garmin Connect first; Google Health does not connect directly to the watch. Google also documents Samsung Galaxy, Xiaomi/Mi Fitness, Oura, Whoop, Strava, and MyFitnessPal connections. On iPhone the route is generally Apple Health. Available types differ by app: a direct Strava connection exports Google Health activities to Strava; importing Strava activities uses Health Connect or Apple Health instead. Google Health supports more types than this Nocturne connector, so check the importable-type table below."

