#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Open the Google Setup documentation linked below. Click its blue button labelled Enable the API and get an OAuth 2.0 Client ID. Use a Google account that can manage your Cloud project. If Google restricts access for your project, resolve that eligibility before continuing. Leave Nocturne open in another tab."
msgstr "Open the Google Setup documentation linked below. Click its blue button labelled Enable the API and get an OAuth 2.0 Client ID. Use a Google account that can manage your Cloud project. If Google restricts access for your project, resolve that eligibility before continuing. Leave Nocturne open in another tab."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Open the Google Setup documentation"
msgstr "Open the Google Setup documentation"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Name your project and enable the API"
msgstr "Name your project and enable the API"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose a new project and enter a project name, or select an existing project you manage. The name is a reminder for you later: any recognisable name is fine. Click Next. Confirm that you want to enable the Google Health API and continue. This enables access to Google's service; it does not create or import any health records."
msgstr "Choose a new project and enter a project name, or select an existing project you manage. The name is a reminder for you later: any recognisable name is fine. Click Next. Confirm that you want to enable the Google Health API and continue. This enables access to Google's service; it does not create or import any health records."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose a product name"
msgstr "Choose a product name"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Enter the product/application name requested by the wizard. You are free to choose it: it may match the project name or be completely different. It is the name shown on Google's consent screen when you connect from Nocturne. Complete any required contact details. Neither name needs to match your Nocturne hostname."
msgstr "Enter the product/application name requested by the wizard. You are free to choose it: it may match the project name or be completely different. It is the name shown on Google's consent screen when you connect from Nocturne. Complete any required contact details. Neither name needs to match your Nocturne hostname."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "For Where are you calling from? select Web Server. In the manual Clients screen the equivalent type is Web application. Copy the complete Callback URL shown by this Nocturne instance under Settings → Connectors & Apps → Google Health into the wizard's redirect field (Authorized redirect URIs). Use your own instance's URL, including its scheme, hostname, port, and callback path exactly. Replace any sample redirect from Google's guide. Click Create. If the wizard's layout changes, the essential choices remain a web client and that exact redirect."
msgstr "For Where are you calling from? select Web Server. In the manual Clients screen the equivalent type is Web application. Copy the complete Callback URL shown by this Nocturne instance under Settings → Connectors & Apps → Google Health into the wizard's redirect field (Authorized redirect URIs). Use your own instance's URL, including its scheme, hostname, port, and callback path exactly. Replace any sample redirect from Google's guide. Click Create. If the wizard's layout changes, the essential choices remain a web client and that exact redirect."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Download the client configuration and fill Nocturne's fields"
msgstr "Download the client configuration and fill Nocturne's fields"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Download the Client configuration/Credentials JSON. Copy Client ID and Client secret into the fields of the same names on Nocturne's Google Health page. The secret is required on first setup; leave it empty only when keeping a secret that was already saved. Check the Callback URL and choose Import data from for the history you want. Keep this form ready while you add the test user in the next step. Store the downloaded file privately: it contains credentials."
msgstr "Download the Client configuration/Credentials JSON. Copy Client ID and Client secret into the fields of the same names on Nocturne's Google Health page. The secret is required on first setup; leave it empty only when keeping a secret that was already saved. Check the Callback URL and choose Import data from for the history you want. Keep this form ready while you add the test user in the next step. Store the downloaded file privately: it contains credentials."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Add the Google account as a test user"
msgstr "Add the Google account as a test user"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Return to the Google Setup documentation, find Add test users, and open its Audience page link. Select the project you just configured. For a personal test use External with publishing status Testing. Under Test users choose Add users, enter the exact email address used in the Google Health app on your phone, and Save. Add each account that will share data. The account managing the Cloud project can be different from the account sharing health data."
msgstr "Return to the Google Setup documentation, find Add test users, and open its Audience page link. Select the project you just configured. For a personal test use External with publishing status Testing. Under Test users choose Add users, enter the exact email address used in the Google Health app on your phone, and Save. Add each account that will share data. The account managing the Cloud project can be different from the account sharing health data."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Check the read permissions in Data Access"
msgstr "Check the read permissions in Data Access"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "In Google's Data Access page choose Add or remove scopes, select the Google Health read scopes shown in Nocturne's reference table below, then Update and Save. Nocturne adds basic sign-in identification itself. These scopes govern which records it can read; they do not allow Nocturne to write to your Google Health account."
msgstr "In Google's Data Access page choose Add or remove scopes, select the Google Health read scopes shown in Nocturne's reference table below, then Update and Save. Nocturne adds basic sign-in identification itself. These scopes govern which records it can read; they do not allow Nocturne to write to your Google Health account."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Save and connect with the same account"
msgstr "Save and connect with the same account"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Return to the prepared Nocturne form and choose Save and connect (or Sign in with Google for an existing configuration). Choose the Google Health account you added as a test user, review and grant the read permissions for the data you want, and confirm you return to Nocturne. Testing grants can expire after seven days and then need reconnection."
msgstr "Return to the prepared Nocturne form and choose Save and connect (or Sign in with Google for an existing configuration). Choose the Google Health account you added as a test user, review and grant the read permissions for the data you want, and confirm you return to Nocturne. Testing grants can expire after seven days and then need reconnection."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "In the available-data table, Found means records exist at the source, not that they have been imported. Select supported types and choose Save selection and import. Save import settings only saves; Refresh inventory only checks availability. Not scanned needs a refreshed inventory; No permission needs the relevant consent; No destination yet is unsupported. Leaving the page does not cancel the server import."
msgstr "In the available-data table, Found means records exist at the source, not that they have been imported. Select supported types and choose Save selection and import. Save import settings only saves; Refresh inventory only checks availability. Not scanned needs a refreshed inventory; No permission needs the relevant consent; No destination yet is unsupported. Leaving the page does not cancel the server import."

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Confirm the result in your reports"
msgstr "Confirm the result in your reports"

#: src/lib/help/connectors.svelte.ts
msgid "Watch sync status and Historical import progress. Open Steps, Heart Rate, or Sleep and choose dates containing source records; use Weight history for weight. If empty, check the source account's visible records, granted permissions, import selection, dates, and last error. Google may still be syncing older phone records; wait for that to finish before retrying. Completed historical months that receive records later need the recovery procedure below."
